Q. What is the benefit of using Service in Kubenetes?
Ans: In Kubernetes, a Service is an abstraction that provides a stable network endpoint to expose a group of Pods running an application. 
Since Pods are ephemeral and their IP addresses can change dynamically, Services ensure consistent access to these Pods without requiring
clients to track their IP changes.

Q. Key Features of Kubernetes Services
*Stable Endpoint*: Services provide a fixed IP address (ClusterIP) and DNS name, ensuring reliable communication with Pods, even as Pods 
are created or destroyed.
*Load Balancing*: Services distribute incoming traffic across multiple Pods, ensuring efficient utilization and high availability.
*Service Discovery*: Kubernetes supports service discovery via DNS or environment variables, allowing clients to locate and connect to 
Services easily.

Q. Types of Services
*ClusterIP*: The default type, accessible only within the cluster. It provides an internal IP for communication between Pods.
*NodePort*: Exposes the Service on a static port on each Node, allowing external access via <NodeIP>:<NodePort>.
*LoadBalancer*: Integrates with cloud providers to provision an external load balancer, exposing the Service to the internet.
*ExternalName*: Maps the Service to an external DNS name, redirecting traffic outside the cluster.
*Headless Service*: Does not assign a ClusterIP, enabling direct communication with individual Pods.

